[{"category":"section","location":"api/#API","page":"API","text":"","title":"API"},{"category":"type","location":"api/#BIOMFormat.BIOMTable","page":"API","text":"BIOMTable\n\nA BIOM table: counts (or other values) of observations (OTUs, ASVs, genes, ...) in samples, with optional metadata on each.\n\nid, type, generated_by, creation_date: the file's header. type is BIOM's controlled vocabulary, e.g. \"OTU table\".\nobservations, samples: the ids, in row and column order.\ndata: the values, a sparse observations × samples matrix (Int when every value is a whole number, else Float64).\nobservation_metadata, sample_metadata: one Dict{String,Any} per id, or nothing when the file has none. A lineage is stored as a vector of ranks under \"taxonomy\".\nobservation_group_metadata, sample_group_metadata: values describing a whole axis, e.g. a phylogeny, as name => (data_type, value).\n\nConstruct one with BIOMTable(data, observations, samples; kwargs...), or read one with read_biom.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"BIOMFormat.BIOMTable"},{"category":"method","location":"api/#BIOMFormat.BIOMTable-Tuple{AbstractMatrix{<:Real}, AbstractVector, AbstractVector}","page":"API","text":"BIOMTable(data, observations, samples; id = \"\", type = \"OTU table\",\n          generated_by = \"BIOMFormat.jl\", creation_date = now,\n          observation_metadata = nothing, sample_metadata = nothing,\n          observation_group_metadata = Dict(), sample_group_metadata = Dict())\n\nA table from an observations × samples matrix (dense or sparse) and the ids. Metadata is one Dict per id, or a vector of Dicts keyed by anything string turns into a key.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"BIOMFormat.BIOMTable"},{"category":"method","location":"api/#BIOMFormat.group_metadata-Tuple{BIOMTable, Symbol}","page":"API","text":"group_metadata(t, axis) -> Dict{String,Tuple{String,String}}\n\nMetadata describing a whole axis (:observation or :sample), such as a phylogeny: name => (data_type, value), e.g. \"phylogeny\" => (\"newick\", \"(...);\").\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"BIOMFormat.group_metadata"},{"category":"method","location":"api/#BIOMFormat.observation_metadata-Tuple{BIOMTable, Any}","page":"API","text":"observation_metadata(t, key) -> Vector\nsample_metadata(t, key) -> Vector\n\nThe value of one metadata field for every observation or sample, with missing where an id has none.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"BIOMFormat.observation_metadata"},{"category":"method","location":"api/#BIOMFormat.observations-Tuple{BIOMTable}","page":"API","text":"observations(t::BIOMTable) -> Vector{String}\nsamples(t::BIOMTable) -> Vector{String}\n\nThe observation (row) and sample (column) ids.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"BIOMFormat.observations"},{"category":"method","location":"api/#BIOMFormat.read_biom-Tuple{AbstractString}","page":"API","text":"read_biom(path) -> BIOMTable\nread_biom(io::IO) -> BIOMTable\n\nRead a BIOM table. Both BIOM 2.1 (HDF5, what QIIME 2 exports) and BIOM 1.0 (JSON) are read from a path, the format told from the file's first bytes; from an IO, only JSON.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"BIOMFormat.read_biom"},{"category":"method","location":"api/#BIOMFormat.write_biom-Tuple{AbstractString, BIOMTable}","page":"API","text":"write_biom(path, t::BIOMTable; format = :hdf5)\nwrite_biom(io::IO, t::BIOMTable)\n\nWrite t as BIOM 2.1 (format = :hdf5, the default) or BIOM 1.0 (format = :json). An IO gets JSON. BIOM 1.0 has no group metadata, so a table with some warns that it is dropped.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"BIOMFormat.write_biom"},{"category":"method","location":"api/#DataAPI.metadata-Tuple{BIOMTable, Symbol}","page":"API","text":"metadata(t, axis) -> Vector{String}\n\nThe metadata fields present on axis (:observation or :sample).\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"DataAPI.metadata"},{"category":"section","location":"#BIOMFormat.jl","page":"Home","text":"See the API for every exported function.","title":"BIOMFormat.jl"},{"category":"module","location":"#BIOMFormat","page":"Home","text":"BIOMFormat\n\nRead and write BIOM tables, the Biological Observation Matrix format of QIIME, QIIME 2, phyloseq and most other amplicon tools: both BIOM 1.0 (JSON) and BIOM 2.1 (HDF5).\n\nusing BIOMFormat\nt = read_biom(\"feature-table.biom\")     # format detected from the file\ncounts(t)                               # observations × samples, sparse\ntaxonomy(t)                             # per-observation lineage, if present\nwrite_biom(\"out.biom\", t)               # BIOM 2.1; `format = :json` for 1.0\n\nWith DenoiseDNA loaded, BIOMTable(seqtab) and SequenceTable(t) convert to and from its sequence tables.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"BIOMFormat"}]
